  'Fountain Branch Carter finished this brick farmhouse in 1830. In the Battle of Franklin on November 30, 1864 it was the Union headquarters of Jacob Cox\'s corps, and the Carter family hid in the basement while the fighting went on round it. His son Tod, a Confederate officer, was brought home mortally wounded and died there on December 2. The State of Tennessee has owned it since it was bought in 1953 to save it from demolition.',
